# %% markdown cell 12f8ae6fd19d7e3d
+### Propagated extraction uncertainties
+
+The reduction inputs are accumulated electrons with a `VARIANCE` image from source, sky, dark and read noise. Each arm uses the explicitly configured independent integrations and an equal-time independently drawn blank. Their accumulated counts and variances are combined before extraction. LmAPD photon variance is $F$ times the detected photon signal; dark and effective read variance are added separately. Native noisy detector frames are preserved in `native/`.
+
+Optimal extraction retains the regularized fitted spatial profile and slit tilt. Its covariance includes the profile fit and shared pixels in overlapping swaths. The displayed uncertainties condition on the measured trace, wavelength solution and calibration products. Median filtering below is only for display; it does not set spectral resolution or define a binned S/N.
+
