+# Kilonova observations and extraction with X-shooter
+
+This companion to `01_Kilonovae.ipynb` starts with a flat AB continuum control, then runs the same Kasen transient plus displaced host at 1.5, 7.5 and 20 rest-frame days. Both faint-continuum and higher-resolution X-shooter settings are simulated and reduced with the prototype DRP.
+
+Both notebooks request dark sky at airmass 1.3 and seeing .70 arcsec. X-shooter uses MJD 60310.25; the ZShooter helper currently drops that requested key when it is absent from the initial commands, so the saved ZShooter frames use their resolved dark-sky date. See the operating-point assessment for that separate parameter-forwarding issue. Telescope, slit, throughput, detector sampling and effective read noise remain instrument-specific. Prepared images contain accumulated electrons and explicit per-pixel variance, including an independently drawn blank exposure. Native ADU frames are saved separately.
+
+Outputs go to `xshooter_kilonova_detectors/`; the earlier runs are preserved. Flux-calibrated science includes host light. The transient-only reference is labeled accordingly; the flat AB control is the clean technical flux test.
+
+**Runtime repair (2026-10-20):** all three epochs now extract and stitch in both modes, and the comparison figures have been regenerated from the saved stochastic frames. UVB's cycling uncertainty refinement is repaired without changing its estimator or tolerance. The **faint-mode NIR flux calibration remains invalid**: its flat-AB control has large spikes associated with unity-valued blaze samples near order ends. The other five mode/arm controls remain close to unity. See [the runtime assessment](../docs/notebook-runtime-checks.md) and [detector operating points](../docs/detector-operating-points.md#reduction-and-verification).
